      "content": "The technocrats' call for global cooperation is nothing but a thinly veiled attempt to maintain their grip on power, distracting us from the fact that their own hubris has crippled our nation's ability to self-sustain. By relying on foreign parts, they're essentially outsourcing our security and leaving our own critical infrastructure – the lifeblood of our economy – to rust and decay. Meanwhile, they're too busy pontificating about \"global governance\" to notice the country's own resources are being drained, its people are being ignored, and its sovereignty is being eroded. It's a classic case of \"we're all in this together,\" except for the fact that we're not – and those who are truly in charge are too blinded by their own ideology to see it.",
      "source": "target",
